title Season G eleventh rung — Ed25519 signature verification in pure Rye
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Rye-first crypto-parity wave; Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; approve your own design rounds and make progress before panicking to check in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop only at custody gates. baton prin recur.
think With scalar reduction mod L GREEN and sent (tenth rung, HEAD 7f1f40acfe), every arithmetic piece the Ed25519 verify equation needs now stood GREEN — decode, the scalar ladder, the group law, scalar reduction mod L, and SHA-512. The crux is the verify assembly itself, and it is non-gated: verification reads only public values (public key, message, signature), holds no secret, and signs nothing. Signing needs a secret scalar and stays the custody gate; verifying is arithmetic anyone can replay.
think Read Zig's std.crypto.sign.Ed25519 verifier to match the exact form: verifyStrict does the cofactorless equation [S]B = R + [k]A with k = reduce64(SHA-512(R || A || M)), rejecting non-canonical S. I implemented the same: refuse non-canonical S via my scalar.is_canonical, decode A via my point decode, recompute k via my sha512 + scalar.reduce, form R' = sub(scalarmul(B,S), scalarmul(A,k)) over the group law, and accept only when to_bytes(R') equals the signature's R bytes — the standard byte-compare, equivalent to verifyStrict's point comparison on valid and tampered signatures.
think Scoping decision to keep this one keystone in one file: rather than expose streaming SHA-512 (its own later rung), verify concatenates R || A || M into one bounded stack buffer capped at a named max_verify_message_bytes (64 KiB) and refuses MessageTooLong beyond — honest and named; a streaming hash for larger payloads is booked as a later rung.
think Derived the base point B rather than pasting its encoding: B has y = 4/5 with even x, so decoding the canonical encoding of y = 4/5 (sign bit clear) recovers exactly B in our own arithmetic. Added a selftest assert that to_bytes(base_point()) equals Zig's basePoint byte-for-byte, so the derivation is proven, not assumed.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass. RFC 8032 section 7.1 TEST 1 (empty message) and TEST 2 (one byte) both accept, a one-bit tamper of each refused. Across 25 cases (5 deterministic Zig keypairs x 5 messages) every genuine signature accepts, every one-byte tamper is refused with the verdict matching Zig's verifyStrict, and a genuine signature refuses against a wrong message. The derived base point matched the standard exactly.
obs Cleaned a first-draft clumsiness in the tamper cross-check: rebuilt a Zig Signature from the tampered bytes via Signature.fromBytes and asked its verifyStrict the same question, so the rejection verdicts are compared honestly rather than left as dead code.
obs tame_style bans clean; the new file lands in none of the ratchet lists. Calls no std.crypto in the primitive. Honest scope held: verification reads only public values, so no key, no signing, no network, no funds, no real device — no custody gate crossed. The signing side is the one remaining Ed25519 piece and it stays the gate.
loom witness=crypto_ed25519_verify_witness rfc_kats=2 keypairs=5 messages=5 genuine=25 tamper=25 result=GREEN
file crypto/ed25519_verify.rye Ed25519 signature verification in pure Rye, composition of the GREEN curve rungs, parity-GREEN vs RFC 8032 and Zig
file tools/crypto_ed25519_verify_witness.rish the witness that builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN line
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md living edge updated to ELEVEN primitives GREEN; git nib refreshed in this work commit
recommend keep-going A Rye-native Ed25519 verifier now stands whole — Lotus signed carry, Kumara identity, Vault, and Comlink can check a signature with no std.crypto or C library. The remaining Ed25519 piece is signing (keygen A = a·B and R = r·B, S = r + k·a), which needs a secret scalar; building and witnessing the signing arithmetic against Zig-generated keypairs is non-gated, while signing with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate. The adjacent non-gated crux is X25519 key agreement over the same GREEN base field. Next durable rung: whichever of those, or the Monocypher-source parity once the vendor fetch clears.
